{
  "title": "Emergent Abilities of Large Language Models",
  "authors": "Wei, Tay, Bommasani, Raffel, Zoph, Borgeaud, Yogatama, Bosma, Zhou, Metzler, Chi, Hashimoto, Vinyals, Liang, Dean, Fedus",
  "year": 2022,
  "venue": "Transactions on Machine Learning Research (TMLR)",
  "summary": "This paper introduces and characterizes \"emergent abilities\" of large language models \u2014 capabilities that are absent in smaller models but appear, often abruptly, once model scale (parameters, compute, or data) crosses a critical threshold. The authors survey dozens of tasks across multiple model families (GPT-3, LaMDA, PaLM, Chinchilla) and show sharp, non-linear performance transitions as a function of scale, arguing that such phase-transition-like behavior cannot be predicted by extrapolating smaller-model performance. The work has become the canonical reference for the phenomenon of emergence in LLMs and sparked subsequent debate (e.g., Schaeffer et al. 2023) about whether emergence is real or a metric artifact.",
